      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gerrit\u0027s pool is a QueuedThreadPool (a Jetty SizedThreadPool), so Jetty uses max(1, min(processors/2, maxThreads/16)), see: [1].\n\nWith the default httpd.maxThreads \u003d 25, 25/16 \u003d 1, so the derived count is 1 selector and does not start to scale with the machine until maxThreads reaches 32 (32/16 \u003d 2).\n\n\n```suggestion\nhttpd.selectorThreads (default 0, meaning Jetty derives the count as\nmax(1, min(processors/2, httpd.maxThreads/16)) for Gerrit\u0027s sized thread\npool). Note that with the default httpd.maxThreads \u003d 25 this resolves to\na single selector; raise httpd.maxThreads for the count to scale with\nCPUs.\n```\n\n[1]: https://github.com/jetty/jetty.project/blob/jetty-12.1.x/jetty-core/jetty-io/src/main/java/org/eclipse/jetty/io/SelectorManager.java#L68-L77",
