      "writtenOn": "2026-08-28T20:39:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Jetty leases executor threads for both acceptors and selectors via ThreadPoolBudget,\n\u003e so raising httpd.selectorThreads (or acceptorThreads) may require raising\n\u003e httpd.maxThreads too.\n\nRight, we haven\u0027t been accounting for thread leasing in the QueuedThreadPool maxThreads count. We probably want to do something like [the trick](https://jetty.org/docs/jetty/12.1/programming-guide/arch/threads.html#thread-pool-configuration) with starting the server and calling `getMaxLeasedThreads()` so that we don\u0027t have to hardcode the reserved threads to a specific number (and `reservedThreads` should probably also be a Gerrit config). That seems like a thing to do in a follow up change.",
      "parentUuid": "064ece89_8a994673",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3700,
        "startChar": 0,
